      "message": "Values are located purely by their positional index among all \u003cdd\u003e elements. The mapping (hostname, id, link, ipv4, dhcp) is encoded only in a comment, not in the selector.\n\nIf OverviewNetwork.vue\u0027s template is ever reordered or a \u003cdd\u003e is added/removed, the tests will silently assert against the wrong field (or shift) rather than failing meaningfully — they\u0027re coupled to DOM layout rather than to the data they claim to verify. The repo already demonstrates the more robust approach: ProfileSettings.spec.js:69 targets specific data-test-id values. The component currently has no test ids, so this is an acceptable tradeoff for a test-only patch — noting it so a follow-up can firm it up if the card grows.\n\nRecommendation: Acceptable as-is for this scope. If tightening later, prefer stable selectors over index destructuring, e.g. add data-test-id to the relevant \u003cdd\u003es and query by them\n\n```\nexpect(wrapper.get(\u0027[data-test-id\u003d\"overviewNetwork-value-interface\"]\u0027).text()).toBe(\u0027eth1\u0027);\n```",
